# Flow Trial / Glance environment template
#
# Placeholders only. Do not put real API keys, tokens, client secrets, or
# service-role keys in this file or anywhere else in git.
#
# These names are what the code already reads. They back Flow Trial / Glance
# (flow-landing Netlify functions and the Glance extension): signup email,
# lead storage, connector OAuth, and the optional Draft-It assist call.
# They are not Flow enterprise controls. This file does not configure SSO,
# an audit log, a DPA, or a private tenant. See docs/product-architecture.md.
#
# Where to set them:
# - Netlify site environment (the flow-landing site). Setting a name here
#   does not set it for Supabase.
# - Supabase Edge Function secrets, only for the two names called out in
#   the last section. The landing pages call Netlify functions, not
#   supabase/functions/send-waitlist-welcome.
#
# Copying this file to .env does not configure production. .gitignore
# ignores .env and .env.* except this example.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Signup, email, and lead storage (Netlify) — required for those paths
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# HMAC secret for confirmation links and the trial download link.
# Read by: confirm-signup, download-trial-zip, send-confirmation,
# send-trial-access, send-playbook, submit-waitlist, check-email-config.
EMAIL_VERIFY_SECRET=replace-with-email-verify-secret

# Resend transactional email. The same NAME is also read by the Supabase
# edge function below; that copy has to be set in Supabase secrets.
# Read by (Netlify): send-confirmation, send-trial-access, send-playbook,
# confirm-signup, submit-lead, check-email-config.
RESEND_API_KEY=replace-with-resend-api-key

# Service-role key for whichever Supabase project the landing functions
# are supposed to write to. The code does not read a URL from the
# environment: submit-lead, submit-waitlist, submit-catch, and
# confirm-signup hardcode SB_URL, and trial.html hardcodes the same URL
# plus a public anon key. supabase/config.toml names a different
# project_id, and src/integrations/supabase/client.ts hardcodes that
# other project. Which project this key must belong to is FM-09. Do not
# put a project URL, project id, or a real key in this file.
# Read by: submit-lead, submit-waitlist, submit-catch, confirm-signup.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=replace-with-supabase-service-role-key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Glance Draft-It and attachment assist (Netlify)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Read by: glance-assist. If unset, the handler reports not-configured.
# The model id is a hardcoded string in that file (owner TODO), not an
# environment variable.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=replace-with-anthropic-api-key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Product telemetry (Netlify) — optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Read by: track-event. If unset, the function accepts the event and
# no-ops. The GA4 measurement id is hardcoded in the landing pages and
# in track-event.js. It is public and is not an environment variable.
GA4_MP_API_SECRET=replace-with-ga4-measurement-protocol-secret

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Connector OAuth (Netlify)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Each *_CLIENT_ID is public (same idea as a GA4 measurement id) and must
# match the client id shipped in the extension. Each *_CLIENT_SECRET stays
# only in Netlify. Never paste a secret into the extension.
#
# On this branch the extension-side public ids are the YOUR_* constants at
# the top of flow-trial-extension/src/background.js:
#   YOUR_HUBSPOT_CLIENT_ID
#   YOUR_SALESFORCE_CLIENT_ID
#   YOUR_SLACK_CLIENT_ID
#   YOUR_MONDAY_CLIENT_ID
# Open PR #21 moves those placeholders to
# flow-trial-extension/config/oauth.public.js and documents the same
# Netlify secret names in flow-trial-extension/docs/SETUP.md. It does not
# add this file. Notion has no server env var: the user pastes their own
# integration token in the extension.

# Read by: hubspot-oauth-exchange, hubspot-oauth-refresh, check-email-config.
HUBSPOT_CLIENT_ID=replace-with-hubspot-public-client-id
HUBSPOT_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-with-hubspot-client-secret

# Read by: salesforce-oauth-exchange, salesforce-oauth-refresh.
SALESFORCE_CLIENT_ID=replace-with-salesforce-public-client-id
SALESFORCE_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-with-salesforce-client-secret

# Read by: slack-oauth-exchange. There is no Slack refresh function.
SLACK_CLIENT_ID=replace-with-slack-public-client-id
SLACK_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-with-slack-client-secret

# Read by: monday-oauth-exchange, monday-oauth-refresh.
MONDAY_CLIENT_ID=replace-with-monday-public-client-id
MONDAY_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-with-monday-client-secret

# Optional. Comma-separated Chrome extension ids in addition to the pinned
# sideload id already allowed in code. Empty is valid.
# Read by: hubspot-oauth-exchange, salesforce-oauth-exchange,
# slack-oauth-exchange, monday-oauth-exchange.
EXTRA_EXTENSION_IDS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase Edge Function secrets (not the Netlify site)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# supabase/functions/send-waitlist-welcome/index.ts
# RESEND_API_KEY — same name as above; set it again in Supabase if this
#   function is deployed. FROM_ADDRESS in that file is still a hardcoded
#   placeholder, not an environment variable.
# WAITLIST_WEBHOOK_SECRET — optional. If unset, the function does not
#   check a webhook header.

WAITLIST_WEBHOOK_SECRET=replace-with-waitlist-webhook-secret

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Names this surface does not read (do not add values for them here)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY — hardcoded, and the two project refs
#   disagree (FM-09). Not process.env.
# VITE_* — the root Vite app does not read import.meta.env.
# Stripe, SSO, audit-log, or tenant secrets — not implemented in this repo.
